  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [prepared_runtime_profile] is cantor-prepared-runtime/0.1
  + [activation_state] is active_for_bounded_implementation_and_evidence
  + [implementation_language] is safe Rust edition 2024

& [AuthorityBoundary] is non-waivable
  = must: preserve execute_protocol_request as the direct deterministic oracle
  = must: use independently supplied request environment digest and complete package bindings before cached semantic use
  = must: preserve exact requested_scope admission
  = must: preserve exact ProtocolResponse status, exit_class, result, faults, proof, continuation, ordering, and digests
  = must: keep physical preparation and synchronization outside semantic meaning
  = must: keep canonical JSON persistence unchanged
  - never: let PreparedRuntime mint caller, purpose, effect, scope, package, trust, or semantic authority
  - never: activate Phase7, neural routing, FPGA execution, database mutation, distributed runtime, or model-hidden-state work through this slice

& [RuntimeGeneration] is immutable semantic input identity
  + [environment] is one immutable EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment
  + [environment_digest] is the exact canonical digest of environment
  + [generation_id] is the digest of prepared_runtime_profile, protocol version, environment version, and environment_digest
  + [pinned_trust_time] is environment now_epoch_seconds
  + [package_order] is environment package vector order and remains digest-significant
  + [trust_state] is embedded TrustStore content and remains subordinate to independent request bindings
  + [lifecycle] is candidate, active, superseded, invalidated, or rolled_back
  = must: create a different generation when any bound input changes
  - never: mutate generation identity or environment in place

& [ScopeProjection] is one immutable admitted runtime view
  + [scope] is one structurally exact AuthorityScope
  + [fabric] is SemanticFabric built from packages admitted under scope
  + [admitted_package_ids] is the deterministic fabric package identity set
  + [projection_key] is generation_id plus canonical exact scope
  + [freshness] is current only for the owning generation and exact scope
  = must: retain at most one projection in this profile
  = must: rebuild and replace the complete projection when scope differs
  - never: reuse a projection for a broader, narrower, overlapping, or similar scope

& [PreparedRuntime] is the core request director
  + [source_environment] is immutable shared ownership retained for exact fallback and scope re-preparation
  + [generation] is RuntimeGeneration metadata
  + [projection_slot] is zero or one immutable ScopeProjection
  + [metrics] is non-authoritative hit, miss, preparation, replacement, and execution observation
  + [interface] is ProtocolRequest to ProtocolResponse
  = must: validate request environment, protocol, caller, purpose, effect, package set, and scope prerequisites before projection use
  = must: share request validation and response construction with direct execution
  = must: release projection coordination locks before query or inspection execution
  = must: return the exact direct response for every accepted request and every constructible fault path
  = must: replace only a complete projection

& [PreparedRuntimeSlot] is whole-generation activation
  + [active_generation] is zero or one complete PreparedRuntime
  + [execute] is acquire one immutable generation snapshot and release the slot lock before semantic execution
  + [replace] is compare expected current generation then atomically install a fully constructed replacement
  + [invalidate] is compare expected current generation then atomically remove it
  + [replace_or_invalidate] is install a valid demanded replacement or deactivate when demanded security-state preparation fails
  + [rollback] is prepare an independently supplied prior environment and activate it as another complete transition
  + [transition_receipt] is previous generation, next generation, disposition, and fault when present
  = must: reject stale expected-generation transitions
  = must: make every new acquisition observe either the complete prior state or complete next state
  = may: let an already acquired immutable request snapshot finish against its exact generation
  - never: silently keep stale authority active after a demanded revocation, staleness, trust-time, or package replacement fails

& [TrustTimeBoundary] is deterministic and explicit
  + [current_authority] is the pinned now_epoch_seconds inside EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment
  + [time_update] is a new environment generation and digest
  + [live_clock] is not implemented
  + [supervisor_obligation] is publish and activate a new trusted-time generation when validity interpretation must change
  - never: claim PreparedRuntime independently enforces wall-clock certificate expiry

& [MemoryBoundary] is measured and bounded
  + [baseline] is the same resident environment without retained admitted fabric
  + [retained] is baseline plus at most one scope projection and coordination metadata
  + [peak] is maximum live heap during preparation and replacement
  + [measurement] is allocation-level retained and peak bytes from isolated repeatable processes
  = must: report absolute bytes and comparable ratios
  = must: evaluate memory and lifecycle cost with latency gain before adapter activation
  - never: use serialized JSON bytes as heap evidence
  - never: introduce an unbounded scope cache

& [ConcurrencyBoundary] is snapshot-safe
  + [reader] is query or inspection over one acquired immutable generation and projection
  + [writer] is projection preparation, generation replacement, invalidation, or rollback
  + [visibility] is old-or-new whole state only
  = must: prove deterministic concurrent reads
  = must: prove replacement and invalidation cannot expose partial state
  = must: prove semantic execution occurs after coordination lock release
  - never: claim distributed, realtime, fairness, or lock-free guarantees

& [ProtocolEquivalenceGate] is PR-AC5 and PR-AC6
  + [query_matrix] is success, partial unresolved, ambiguity, budget exhaustion, invalid request, policy denial, trust failure, proof gap, semantic fault, and internal fault where fixtures can construct them
  + [inspect_matrix] is fabric, package, certificate, semantic-unit success plus invalid, policy, trust, unknown-identity, and proof-gap paths
  + [comparison] is direct ProtocolResponse equality before and after serialization
  + [verification] is verify_protocol_response and deterministic direct re-execution
  - never: accept selected-field or success-only equivalence

& [AdoptionGate] is evidence-driven
  + [correctness] is zero ProtocolResponse, digest, scope, lifecycle, or concurrency mismatch
  + [latency] is warm preparation, cold process preparation, direct repeated request, prepared miss, and prepared hit measured separately
  + [memory] is retained and peak allocation measured over representative multi-shape fixtures
  + [complexity] is lifecycle, synchronization, fault, dependency, and adapter surface recorded
  + [disposition] is activate, retain_core_only, revise, or reject
  = must: select disposition from the complete evidence set
  = must: preserve direct request-scoped execution as rollback
  - never: activate merely because a prepared query microbenchmark is fast

& [AcceptanceGate] is PR-AC1 through PR-AC14
  @ [definition] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Prepared_Runtime.exploded.sop

